# Exhaustion of the seven-point double cosets

The table factors every permutation as an even Sylow element, one of the
98 representatives, and another even Sylow element. Its order follows
Mathlib's `permsOfList`; `List.Forall₂` checks every row by kernel reduction.
The permutation enumeration theorem then gives coverage of the entire S₇.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
13.8.24, printed pp.958–959; this is the explicit finite calculation used
in the fixed-coordinate solvable-overgroup argument.
-/

